.TH MD_GET_CHANNEL 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.2.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_get_channel \- copy a tracked channel summary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

int md_get_channel(const morsedec_decoder_t *decoder, size_t index,
    struct morsedec_channel *channel);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy a tracked channel summary.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.TP
.I index
Zero-based enumeration position, strictly below md_get_channel_count().
.TP
.I channel
Non-NULL output structure; receives a caller-owned copy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns MORSEDEC_SUCCESS (1) on success, or MORSEDEC_FAILURE (0) and sets
errno on failure. Do not inspect errno after success.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
NULL decoder or channel, or index outside the current enumeration.
.SH REMARKS
Copies the channel ID, state, frequency, snr, wpm, key_probability, strength
and character_count. See libmorsedec(3) for field units and interpretation.
Frequencies are FFT-bin centers; on I/Q handles they are signed Hz offsets
from 0 Hz IF.
.PP
The ID remains associated with this channel until retirement or reset.
Enumeration indices can change on any processing call and must not be stored
as identities. Pass channel.id to md_get_text() or md_get_characters(). A
copied summary is not updated when the decoder advances. Enumeration remains
available after flush.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0 (shared-library ABI
1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_get_channel_count (3),
.BR md_get_characters (3),
.BR md_get_text (3),
.BR md_get_state (3)
